      en: "Kassala is the capital of the Region KS state in Sudan. It plays a significant role in regional administration and economy. Agricultural production in the area shapes the cityscape. Administratively part of SD-KS. Serves as the administrative headquarters of the region. Located at coordinates 15.45, 36.4. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Sudan along the Nile, the Nubian Desert and the Red Sea, and offers insight into the ancient Nubian heritage and the regional identity."
